Part of the Perl CLI strand (see the strand card). Covers the Claude hooks.

Port runHookCommand (cli.ts:368-399) and runHook (hooks.ts):
- `--harness X` (codex and hermes are recognised; their behaviour comes with the Codex and Hermes cards).
- stdin: empty on a TTY; malformed JSON is ignored.
- projectDir from SKILLETOR_PROJECT_DIR, else CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR.
- A compact JSON line, printed only when it has a systemMessage or hookSpecificOutput.
- Exit 0 on every failure, as fixed by k164.

session-start:
- check with a 5 s timeout, then markChecked, then a sync when the check says changed;
- on a lock timeout, dueAgain;
- recordSessionCwd.

user-prompt-submit:
- takePendingReport;
- the interval: checkInterval, 600 when the config fails to load;
- a detached background self-spawn of `hook __sync-background`:
  - a PAR binary re-executes $^X; plain perl runs $^X with the script;
  - setsid (so the Hermes killpg spares it); stdio ignored; SKILLETOR_PROJECT_DIR set.

__sync-background: sync, then putPendingReport; on a lock timeout, dueAgain.

